  "rationale": "`Output::quiet()` sets `quiet: true`. Every message helper (`already_ok`, `done`, `added`, `removed`, `info`, `blank`, `println`) goes through `emit`, and `warn` goes through `emit_err`; both return immediately when `self.quiet`, before capturing or printing. There is no other print path in `Output` (`is_interactive` prints nothing). `quiet` and `capture` are only set by the constructors, so a quiet output stays quiet.\n\nTests: indirect only. `tests/hook_stdout.rs` `sync_progress_stays_off_hook_stdout` (passes) runs a real `SessionStart` hook for five agents, whose auto-sync uses `Output::quiet()` (`src/sync.rs:372`), and asserts stdout is valid JSON / free of sync progress. No unit test asserts silence directly; the code is short enough to judge fully.",
  "requirement": "A quiet `Output` MUST NOT print any message."
